The LLM generated a new `mirror_palette_addr` function to normalize palette addresses using mirroring rules, updated palette_table reads and writes to use this function instead of direct indexing, and created a test named `test_ppu_palette_mirroring_3f20_region` to confirm that writes to 0x3F20 correctly mirror to 0x3F00 as expected in NES PPU palette memory behavior.